Time Complexity:

Let n = size of nums1
Let m = size of nums2

    Traverse both arrays once → O(n + m)

Overall: O(n + m)


Space Complexity:

    No extra data structures used

Overall: O(1)


Approach:

1. Initialize two pointers:
   - i = 0 for nums1
   - j = 0 for nums2

2. Traverse both arrays simultaneously:

   - If nums1[i] == nums2[j]:
     → Common element found
     → Return that value

   - If nums1[i] < nums2[j]:
     → Increment i

   - Else:
     → Increment j

3. Continue until one array ends

4. If no common element exists:
   → Return -1



class Solution {
    public int getCommon(int[] nums1, int[] nums2) {
        int i = 0;
        int j = 0;
        while(i<nums1.length && j<nums2.length){
            if(nums1[i]==nums2[j]) return nums2[j];
            if(nums1[i]<nums2[j]) i++;
            else j++;
        } 
        return -1;
    }
}
